A||N||10||Haze_Performance||Anyone with 16" x 7.5" wheels? Or anyone that can help.||||10||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||02-19-2001||11:15 PM||||OK in my last post I needed some tire sizes for a new set of wheels that I bought. I thought they were 16"x7". They came Sat. and they ended up being 16"x7.5" (38mm offset)<P>Im NOT a tire size math wizz.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/24207595_2.jpg">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/172all.jpg"> <P>Can someone help me with some tires sizes? <BR>Im looking to fill the wheel wells a <B>little</B> with a taller tire. But I dont want a <B>HUGE</B> one. Im not going to lower the car at all. I also dont want the tires to overlap the wheels. I would like a flush wheel & tire.<P><BR>TFTS    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Carl<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">   </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>PFF Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1431213" TARGET=_blank><BR>Photopoint Gallery</A><P>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 02-19-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 02-20-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000001||terryk||02-19-2001||11:31 PM||||Use this site for size comparision. I also use tirerack for rims size vs tires size. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.secret-secret.com/turbo/DIY/tirecalc/turbotire.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.secret-secret.com/turbo/DIY/tirecalc/turbotire.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||02-19-2001||11:59 PM||||Haze, What size tire were you going to go with? A 215/50 would look nice on those. You could go to a 235/50 but for handling I'd go 215/50. To fill the wheel well a 225/50 would be nice too. It doesn't matter that they are .5" wider unless you want to go to a wider tire.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Haze_Performance||02-20-2001||12:17 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by terryk:<BR><B>Use this site for size comparision. I also use tirerack for rims size vs tires size. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.secret-secret.com/turbo/DIY/tirecalc/turbotire.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.secret-secret.com/turbo/DIY/tirecalc/turbotire.html</A> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Hmmmm.... Thanks for the link.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><BR>I guess Im looking for 225/55/16 Huh?<BR><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif"> </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>PFF Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1431213" TARGET=_blank><BR>Photopoint Gallery</A>||||reg||14
Z||000004||Haze_Performance||02-20-2001||12:24 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>Haze, What size tire were you going to go with? A 215/50 would look nice on those. You could go to a 235/50 but for handling I'd go 215/50. To fill the wheel well a 225/50 would be nice too. It doesn't matter that they are .5" wider unless you want to go to a wider tire.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well...I would like to have the tires fulsh with the wheels.(No excessive overlap) Im not sure what size to go with. How wide would a 225/50 be on those wheels? Would 225/55 fit better?<P><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif"> </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>PFF Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1431213" TARGET=_blank><BR>Photopoint Gallery</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||02-20-2001||12:49 AM||||I've got 225/50-16's on my Ciera GT. The wheels are 16x7". I sat one up against the Fiero and even with a 1.5" drop, they will clear and fill the wells nicely. <P>225/60-16's are too tall and hit the inside in the front.<P>I want some sidewall to cushion it a bit since I have spherical control arm bearings in the back and it's rather hard.  <P>On the Fiero, I think I'll be going with 225/50-16. Let me know what you decide.  <p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 02-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||02-20-2001||01:13 AM||||Haze, A 225/50 is the same width as a 225/55. It's just that the 225/50 has a 4.4" sidewall and the 55 has a 4.6" sidewall.<BR>215, 225, 235, 245, etc is the tire width. the series (70,60, 50,40, etc) is the precentage of the width that makes the height of the sidewall. So a 225/50 tire is 8.8" wide and the sidewall is 4.4" 225/60 is 8.8" wide and the sidewall is 4.8". The higher the series the higher the sidewall. To keep the speedo close you need to keep the diameter close. Anything that came with the 14" wheels is set-up for 23.9" (215/60R14) I went with a 225/50R15 and my diameter is 23.8" If you went with a 225/50R16 you would be at 24.8" (4.4" for bottom sidewall, 16" for wheel, 4.4" for top sidewall) So the tire would be about an inch taller. This is divided in half so the height of the car would go up 1/2" and the wheel well gap would be smaller by 1/2".  Your speedo would read 2.8% slower than actual speed. So if speedo reads 100mph you would really be doing 102.8mph. 50mph on the speedo would mean your doing 51.4mph.<BR>Hope all this tire babble helps.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">   <P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 02-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula88||02-20-2001||02:54 AM||||Well, to keep the same overall tire diameter, and starting with a 215/60-15, you'd want to go with a 225/50-16.  That will have the same overall tire diameter.  If you want a little taller tire, go with a 235/50-16 instead.  For the fronts, if they started with 205/60-15's, go with either 215/50-16 or 225/50-16's.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Alex4mula||02-20-2001||09:08 AM||||I would strongly recommend you to go to the tirerack.com site and check the "Specs" link on the tires brand you plan to buy. For most sizes you will find the tire diameter size for it. Even maybe for your current brand. When I did that I found out that the same tire size (i.e. 225-40-17) may have different diameters depending on which brand it was. Difference was small (0.1-0.2) but there is. I used their website for this & then bought from DiscountTire  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">!||||reg||1
Z||000009||elfiero||02-20-2001||10:01 AM||||Haze,I used 205/50-16 on the front,225/45-16<BR>on the rear.These were reccomended by tire<BR>rack.com(live person)they fit the <BR>wheel wells perfectlyNOTE;car is lowered<BR>21/2inches||||reg||6
